{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>The good land, the good mountain.</b> They said in the Midrash: a parable of a king who sought to marry a woman and sent his emissaries to see whether she was beautiful or not. They went and saw her and said to him, 'There is none uglier than her.' The matchmaker heard and said to them, 'My masters, there is none more beautiful than her in the world.' He came to marry her. The girl's father said to the king's emissaries, 'I swear that not one of you may enter here, for you have maligned my daughter before the king.' The matchmaker came to enter; he said to him, 'You too shall not enter.' The matchmaker said to him, 'I did not see her and I said to the king, \"There is none in the world more beautiful than her,\" while they said, \"There is none uglier than her.\" Now I shall see her — whether according to my words or according to theirs.' So said Moses before the Holy One, blessed be He: 'Master of the universe! The spies spoke evil speech (lashon ha-ra), as it is said (Numbers 13:32): ״ארץ אוכלת יושביה היא״, and I did not see it and yet I praised it to Israel, as it is said (Deuteronomy 8:7): ״כי ה' אלהיך מביאך אל ארץ טובה״ and so forth; and now I shall see it — whether according to my words or according to theirs, as it is said: אעברה נא ואראה את הארץ הטובה. <b>This good mountain and the Lebanon</b> — this is the Temple, which whitens (מלבין) the transgressions of Israel.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:05.382398835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}